{"author":{"id":"038d65070aa747b6bc9d50939fa697ec871a40ed259db54429b255bbef2581d6"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1793022385,"nonce":"KTA4TIpIFPo5ZKo1pYOU2HgBFCY=","title":"Bound shared-document admission and refuse missing-file reads","message":"Slice of browser session abuse/resource track 080ea85416efa648d8a634f8a1906bdecb0e70bf9da9cf934675d832d8533081.\n\ndoc.open currently loads a missing path as an empty Yrs document and writes recovery state, including for unsigned read-only viewers. The server also retains unbounded unique open documents across connections, despite the page projection's own client-side cap.\n\nRequire an existing text file for doc.open; use fs.write to create a new file explicitly. Apply the existing file-read size limit before document materialization. Enforce limits per connection and across the workspace, count repeated subscriptions once, share existing documents at the workspace limit, reject before state creation, and release admission capacity after close/disconnection. Persist the initial CRDT baseline for existing files so normal offline recovery remains consistent.\n\nValidate signed and unsigned missing paths create no files or state; oversized files fail before state creation; per-connection and workspace limits hold across simultaneous opens and recover after failed opens/close/disconnect; opening at least 65 ordinary code tabs remains supported. Preserve current protocol/editor behavior for existing files. Rebuild/stage WASM and session services for browser testing. This slice does not complete aggregate byte/rate/storage quotas, durable DO document authority or MSB provisioning.","files":null}]}